7.1" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">40</text><text x="205.7" y="274" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">t / s</text><text x="25.4" y="14" font-size="14" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">v / m s⁻¹</text><polyline points="29.4,57.1 221.7,168" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polyline points="221.7,168 349.9,242" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke-dasharray:5 4"/></svg>', 'A straight v–t line falling from 40 m s⁻¹ at t = 0 to 16 m s⁻¹ at 30 s, continued (dashed) at the same gradient to v = 0.'),
('b54dbeea-ad44-5fb3-98de-39acde178240', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '91cb1c54-423a-4525-a723-99c1e9e9bf6b', 'a-level', '2.2', '9702 coursebook 2.2 · Calculating acceleration', 31, 31, 'A sprinter''s speed is 6.0 m s⁻¹ after 1.0 s and 9.6 m s⁻¹ after 2.5 s. Calculate her average acceleration in this interval.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '2.4', 'm s⁻²', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'a = (9.6 − 6.0) ÷ (2.5 − 1.0) = 2.4 m s⁻². Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: Δv. C1: Δt. A1: a = 2.4 m s⁻².', 3, NULL, NULL),
('05fbc54e-9aff-5fbb-8daf-1d6b7545aacf', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '91cb1c54-423a-4525-a723-99c1e9e9bf6b', 'a-level', '2.2', '9702 coursebook 2.2 · Calculating acceleration', 32, 32, 'Which situation has the largest acceleration: A 0 → 20 m s⁻¹ in 4 s; B 10 → 30 m s⁻¹ in 5 s; C 30 → 0 m s⁻¹ in 5 s?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'C (6 m s⁻² in size)', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Compare |Δv|/t: 5, 4 and 6 m s⁻². Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: values. C1: compare magnitudes. A1: D (C (6 m s⁻² in size)).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('46cf1ff7-3ad8-5dd4-a56c-b087fa64aedf', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '91cb1c54-423a-4525-a723-99c1e9e9bf6b', 'a-level', '2.2', '9702 coursebook 2.2 · Calculating acceleration', 33, 33, 'A cyclist freewheels down a hill, accelerating from 4.0 m s⁻¹ at 0.35 m s⁻² for 40 s. Calculate her final speed.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '18', 'm s⁻¹', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'v = 4.0 + 0.35 × 40 = 18 m s⁻¹. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: v = u + at. C1: value. A1: v = 18 m s⁻¹.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('a2e48d54-d50a-5c26-ae7f-45aed1dcc684', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '91cb1c54-423a-4525-a723-99c1e9e9bf6b', 'a-level', '2.2', '9702 coursebook 2.2 · Calculating acceleration', 34, 34, 'An electron is accelerated from 2.0 × 10⁶ m s⁻¹ to 8.0 × 10⁶ m s⁻¹ in 3.0 × 10⁻⁹ s. Calculate its acceleration, in units of 10¹⁵ m s⁻².', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '2', '10¹⁵ m s⁻²', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'a = (8.0 × 10⁶ − 2.0 × 10⁶) ÷ 3.0 × 10⁻⁹ = 2.0 × 10¹⁵ m s⁻². Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: Δv. C1: ÷ t. A1: a = 2.0 × 10¹⁵ m s⁻².', 3, NULL, NULL),
('29c342e3-a684-5de2-a684-cf26a363b64f', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '91cb1c54-423a-4525-a723-99c1e9e9bf6b', 'a-level', '2.2', '9702 coursebook 2.2 · Calculating acceleration', 35, 35, 'A car brakes from 25 m s⁻¹ at 6.5 m s⁻². Calculate its speed 2.0 s after the brakes are applied.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '12', 'm s⁻¹', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'v = 25 − 6.5 × 2.0 = 12 m s⁻¹. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: negative a. C1: value. A1: v = 12 m s⁻¹.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('569a6d30-3e9c-54b7-87f5-914b64506ab0', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '91cb1c54-423a-4525-a723-99c1e9e9bf6b', 'a-level', '2.2', '9702 coursebook 2.2 · Calculating acceleration', 36, 36, 'A car''s velocity is +10 m s⁻¹ and its acceleration is −2 m s⁻². What is its velocity 8 s later if the acceleration stays constant?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, '−6 m s⁻¹', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'v = 10 + (−2) × 8 = −6 m s⁻¹. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: v = u + at. C1: sign. A1: B (−6 m s⁻¹).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('76b67b22-eacb-5797-b556-bf758d33e2b1', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '91cb1c54-423a-4525-a723-99c1e9e9bf6b', 'a-level', '2.2', '9702 coursebook 2.2 · Calculating acceleration', 37, 37, 'A ball thrown upwards at 18 m s⁻¹ decelerates at 9.81 m s⁻². How long does it take to reach its highest point?', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '1.835', 's', false, NULL, false, NULL, 't = 18 ÷ 9.81 = 1.83 s. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: v = 0 at top. C1: t = u/g. A1: t = 1.83 s.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('e48d9ede-d200-57e9-a745-ccda3f547661', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '91cb1c54-423a-4525-a723-99c1e9e9bf6b', 'a-level', '2.2', '9702 coursebook 2.2 · Calculating acceleration', 38, 38, 'A lorry''s speed increases from 15 m s⁻¹ to 21 m s⁻¹ while it travels for 12 s. Calculate its acceleration.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.5', 'm s⁻²', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'a = (21 − 15) ÷ 12 = 0.50 m s⁻². Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: Δv. C1: ÷ t. A1: a = 0.50 m s⁻².', 3, NULL, NULL),
('c7b93af8-dafb-5f60-94b3-052b8bfd404b', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '91cb1c54-423a-4525-a723-99c1e9e9bf6b', 'a-level', '2.2', '9702 coursebook 2.2 · Calculating acceleration', 39, 39, 'A lift accelerates downwards from rest at 0.90 m s⁻². Calculate its speed after 2.5 s.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '2.25', 'm s⁻¹', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'v = 0 + 0.90 × 2.5 = 2.25 m s⁻¹. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: v = u + at. C1: value. A1: v = 2.25 m s⁻¹.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('d90407f3-3b0f-5cd9-a1a8-2f179b4d8347', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '91cb1c54-423a-4525-a723-99c1e9e9bf6b', 'a-level', '2.2', '9702 coursebook 2.2 · Calculating acceleration', 40, 40, 'A car moving at 14 m s⁻¹ accelerates at 1.2 m s⁻² for 7.5 s. Calculate its final speed in km h⁻¹.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '82.8', 'km h⁻¹', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'v = 14 + 1.2 × 7.5 = 23 m s⁻¹. In km h⁻¹: 23 × 3.6 = 82.8. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: v = u + at. C1: × 3.6. A1: v = 82.8 km h⁻¹.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('4f1b9b6f-c7df-54d6-bb4d-c0d9b81df56d', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '91cb1c54-423a-4525-a723-99c1e9e9bf6b', 'a-level', '2.2', '9702 coursebook 2.2 · Calculating acceleration', 41, 41, 'Cars A and B both reach 30 m s⁻¹ from rest; A takes 6.0 s and B takes 10 s. Calculate (acceleration of A) ÷ (acceleration of B).', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '1.667', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'a_A = 30 ÷ 6.0 = 5.0 m s⁻²; a_B = 30 ÷ 10 = 3.0 m s⁻²; ratio = 5.0 ÷ 3.0 = 1.67. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: both. C1: ratio. A1: ratio = 1.67.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('52f59ba6-8a76-5770-ae20-9ccab554bf12', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '91cb1c54-423a-4525-a723-99c1e9e9bf6b', 'a-level', '2.2', '9702 coursebook 2.2 · Calculating acceleration', 42, 42, 'A ball is thrown straight down at 5.0 m s⁻¹ and accelerates at 9.81 m s⁻². Calculate its speed after 1.5 s.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '19.71', 'm s⁻¹', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'v = 5.0 + 9.81 × 1.5 = 19.7 m s⁻¹. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: v = u + at. C1: value. A1: v = 19.7 m s⁻¹.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('f73b3bff-1f65-5cfa-8fde-39740cfb68ae', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '91cb1c54-423a-4525-a723-99c1e9e9bf6b', 'a-level', '2.2', '9702 coursebook 2.2 · Calculating acceleration', 43, 43, 'A car accelerates uniformly from rest. After 3.0 s its speed is 7.5 m s⁻¹. (a) Calculate its acceleration. (b) Calculate its speed after a further 5.0 s at the same acceleration.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '20', 'm s⁻¹', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) a = 7.5 ÷ 3.0 = 2.5 m s⁻². (b) v = 7.5 + 2.5 × 5.0 = 20 m s⁻¹. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: a. C1: value. M1: v = u + at. C1: value. A1: v = 20 m s⁻¹.', 5, NULL, NULL),
('e3716c98-0241-58bf-bbcc-0f707f40a547', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '91cb1c54-423a-4525-a723-99c1e9e9bf6b', 'a-level', '2.2', '9702 coursebook 2.2 · Calculating acceleration', 44, 44, 'A test car crashes into a wall at 15 m s⁻¹ and stops in 0.090 s. A dummy with a seat belt stops in 0.15 s. (a) Calculate the car''s deceleration. (b) Calculate the dummy''s deceleration. (c) Express the dummy''s deceleration in units of g (g = 9.81 m s⁻²).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '10.19', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) a = 15 ÷ 0.090 = 167 m s⁻². (b) a = 15 ÷ 0.15 = 100 m s⁻². (c) 100 ÷ 9.81 = 10.2. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: car. C1: dummy. M1: ÷ g. C1: value. B1: longer time, smaller deceleration. A1: a/g = 10.2.', 6, NULL, NULL),
('ae62846c-69ad-51bf-b86b-56d9935fb299', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '91cb1c54-423a-4525-a723-99c1e9e9bf6b', 'a-level', '2.2', '9702 coursebook 2.2 · Calculating acceleration', 45, 45, 'A train passes signal A at 20 m s⁻¹ and signal B, 50 s later, at 30 m s⁻¹, accelerating uniformly. It keeps accelerating at the same rate. (a) Calculate its acceleration. (b) Calculate its speed 20 s after passing B.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '34', 'm s⁻¹', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) a = (30 − 20) ÷ 50 = 0.20 m s⁻². (b) v = 30 + 0.20 × 20 = 34 m s⁻¹. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: Δv. C1: a. M1: v = u + at. C1: value. A1: v = 34 m s⁻¹.', 5, NULL, NULL),
('4e56c330-2efd-526c-9297-557ada205059', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '91cb1c54-423a-4525-a723-99c1e9e9bf6b', 'a-level', '2.2', '9702 coursebook 2.2 · Calculating acceleration', 46, 46, 'A ball is thrown vertically upwards at 24 m s⁻¹. Taking up as positive and g = 9.81 m s⁻²: (a) calculate the time to the top; (b) calculate its velocity 4.0 s after release; (c) explain the sign.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '-15.24', 'm s⁻¹', false, NULL, true, NULL, '(a) t = 24 ÷ 9.81 = 2.45 s. (b) v = 24 − 9.81 × 4.0 = −15.2 m s⁻¹. (c) Negative: it is moving downwards after passing the top. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: time to top. M1: v = u + at. C1: substitution. C1: value. B1: sign. A1: v = −15.2 m s⁻¹.', 6, NULL, NULL),
('464a6b0e-d435-5575-8270-2dec6b96d8c1', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '91cb1c54-423a-4525-a723-99c1e9e9bf6b', 'a-level', '2.2', '9702 coursebook 2.2 · Calculating acceleration', 47, 47, 'A rocket accelerates from rest at 20 m s⁻² for 15 s, then its engine stops and it decelerates at 9.81 m s⁻². (a) Calculate its speed when the engine stops. (b) Calculate the further time until it stops rising.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '30.58', 's', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) v = 20 × 15 = 300 m s⁻¹. (b) t = 300 ÷ 9.81 = 30.6 s. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: v = at. C1: 300. M1: t = v/g. C1: value. A1: t = 30.6 s.', 5, NULL, NULL),
('961a95cd-10a3-5700-987c-b1f1a0e5e2c7', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '91cb1c54-423a-4525-a723-99c1e9e9bf6b', 'a-level', '2.2', '9702 coursebook 2.2 · Calculating acceleration', 48, 48, 'A car driver reacts in 0.70 s and then brakes at 6.0 m s⁻² from 24 m s⁻¹. (a) Calculate the braking time. (b) Calculate the total time from seeing a hazard to stopping.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '4.7', 's', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) t = 24 ÷ 6.0 = 4.0 s. (b) 0.70 + 4.0 = 4.7 s. Mark scheme (5 marks). M1: t = Δv/a. C1: 4.0 s. M1: add reaction time. C1: value. A1: t = 4.7 s.', 5, NULL, NULL),
('d8fa912a-0941-5576-aa94-4ac2bfab29ed', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '91cb1c54-423a-4525-a723-99c1e9e9bf6b', 'a-level', '2.2', '9702 coursebook 2.2 · Calculating acceleration', 49, 49, 'A lift accelerates upwards at 1.2 m s⁻² for 2.5 s, travels at constant speed for 6.0 s and decelerates to rest in 2.0 s. (a) Calculate the top speed. (b) Calculate the deceleration. (c) Calculate the total time.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '1.5', 'm s⁻²', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) v = 1.2 × 2.5 = 3.0 m s⁻¹. (b) a = 3.0 ÷ 2.0 = 1.5 m s⁻². (c) 2.5 + 6.0 + 2.0 = 10.5 s. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: top speed. M1: a = Δv/t. C1: deceleration. C1: total time. B1: answer (b). A1: a = 1.5 m s⁻².', 6, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fgd0b6718c-t fgd0b6718c-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fgd0b6718c-t">Lift v–t graph</title><desc id="fgd0b6718c-d">A lift v–t graph: a straight rise over 2.5 s, constant speed for 6.0 s and a straight fall to rest over 2.0 s.</desc><line x1="24" y1="34" x2="24" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="89.1" y1="34" x2="89.1" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="154.2" y1="34" x2="154.2" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="219.3" y1="34" x2="219.3" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="284.4" y1="34" x2="284.4" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="349.5" y1="34" x2="349.5" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="24" y1="242" x2="382" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="24" y1="190" x2="382" y2="190" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="24" y1="138" x2="382" y2="138" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="24" y1="86" x2="382" y2="86" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="24" y1="34" x2="382" y2="34" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="24" y1="242" x2="388" y2="242" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="24" y1="242" x2="24" y2="28" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="392,242 385.7,245 385.7,239" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><polygon points="24,24 27,30.3 21,30.3" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><line x1="24" y1="242" x2="24" y2="246" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="24" y="254" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">0</text><line x1="89.1" y1="242" x2="89.1" y2="246" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="89.1" y="254" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">2</text><line x1="154.2" y1="242" x2="154.2" y2="246" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="154.2" y="254" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">4</text><line x1="219.3" y1="242" x2="219.3" y2="246" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="219.3" y="254" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">6</text><line x1="284.4" y1="242" x2="284.4" y2="246" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="284.4" y="254" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">8</text><line x1="349.5" y1="242" x2="349.5" y2="246" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="349.5" y="254" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">10</text><line x1="20" y1="242" x2="24" y2="242" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="17" y="242" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">0</text><line x1="20" y1="190" x2="24" y2="190" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="17" y="190" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">1</text><line x1="20" y1="138" x2="24" y2="138" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="17" y="138" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">2</text><line x1="20" y1="86" x2="24" y2="86" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="17" y="86" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">3</text><line x1="20" y1="34" x2="24" y2="34" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="17" y="34" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">4</text><text x="203" y="274" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">t / s</text><text x="20" y="14" font-size="14" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">v / m s⁻¹</text><polyline points="24,242 105.4,86 300.6,86 365.7,242" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/></svg>', 'A lift v–t graph: a straight rise over 2.5 s, constant speed for 6.0 s and a straight fall to rest over 2.0 s.'),
('63884a84-0d1a-5d9c-9723-b9f07ff9fcd8', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '91cb1c54-423a-4525-a723-99c1e9e9bf6b', 'a-level', '2.2', '9702 coursebook 2.2 · Calculating acceleration', 50, 50, 'A sprinter covers the first 2.0 s of a race with uniform acceleration, reaching 9.0 m s⁻¹. A rival reaches 9.0 m s⁻¹ in 2.4 s. (a) Calculate both accelerations. (b) Calculate their difference.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.75', 'm s⁻²', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) 9.0 ÷ 2.0 = 4.5 m s⁻²; 9.0 ÷ 2.4 = 3.75 m s⁻². (b) 4.5 − 3.75 = 0.75 m s⁻². Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: first. C1: second. M1: difference. C1: value. A1: Δa = 0.75 m s⁻².', 5, NULL, NULL),
('bda50b13-6f0a-5282-893c-d0fba914c3e2', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '91cb1c54-423a-4525-a723-99c1e9e9bf6b', 'a-level', '2.2', '9702 coursebook 2.2 · Calculating acceleration', 51, 51, 'A particle has velocity 6.0 m s⁻¹ east, and 4.0 s later 8.0 m s⁻¹ north. (a) Calculate |Δv|. (b) Calculate the magnitude of its average acceleration. (c) Find the direction of the acceleration as an angle west of north.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '36.87', '°', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) |Δv| = √(6.0² + 8.0²) = 10 m s⁻¹. (b) a = 10 ÷ 4.0 = 2.5 m s⁻². (c) θ = tan⁻¹(6.0 ÷ 8.0) = 36.9°. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: |Δv|. C1: a. M1: components of Δv. M1: tan θ. C1: value. A1: θ = 36.9°.', 6, NULL, NULL),
('4b08168a-9e67-5229-b54a-ce94af8b61d4', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '91cb1c54-423a-4525-a723-99c1e9e9bf6b', 'a-level', '2.2', '9702 coursebook 2.2 · Calculating acceleration', 52, 52, 'A spacecraft''s speed rises from 0 to 1.2 km s⁻¹ in 120 s, then from 1.2 km s⁻¹ to 7.8 km s⁻¹ in 400 s. (a) Calculate each acceleration. (b) Calculate the average acceleration over the 520 s.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '15', 'm s⁻²', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) 1200 ÷ 120 = 10 m s⁻²; (7800 − 1200) ÷ 400 = 16.5 m s⁻². (b) a = 7800 ÷ 520 = 15 m s⁻². Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: first. C1: second. M1: overall Δv/t. C1: value. A1: a = 15 m s⁻².', 5, NULL, NULL)
