('4585beab-377a-5c2b-953c-67ce07097eb3', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '5e4207c2-e358-4374-b5ab-92bbcb2b87e7', 'a-level', '2.4', '9702 coursebook 2.4 · Deducing acceleration', 29, 29, 'Two cars start from rest together. Car A''s v–t graph has gradient 2.0 m s⁻² and car B''s 3.0 m s⁻². What is the difference in their speeds after 6.0 s?', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '6', 'm s⁻¹', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Δv = (3.0 − 2.0) × 6.0 = 6.0 m s⁻¹. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: v = at for each. C1: difference. A1: Δv = 6.0 m s⁻¹.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('281bc377-f15d-5af9-97ee-b9fbf370db86', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '5e4207c2-e358-4374-b5ab-92bbcb2b87e7', 'a-level', '2.4', '9702 coursebook 2.4 · Deducing acceleration', 30, 30, 'What does a v–t graph with a positive but decreasing gradient show about a car?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'It is speeding up, but less and less quickly', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Positive gradient: speeding up; decreasing gradient: smaller acceleration. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: speeding up. C1: acceleration decreasing. A1: B (It is speeding up, but less and less quickly).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('5c8610f9-ffc4-592d-84cd-e85166c1363c', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '5e4207c2-e358-4374-b5ab-92bbcb2b87e7', 'a-level', '2.4', '9702 coursebook 2.4 · Deducing acceleration', 31, 31, 'A v–t graph shows a bouncing ball (up positive) going from −6.0 m s⁻¹ to +4.5 m s⁻¹ in 0.030 s at the bounce. Calculate the average acceleration during the bounce.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '350', 'm s⁻²', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'a = (4.5 − (−6.0)) ÷ 0.030 = 350 m s⁻². Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: Δv = 10.5. C1: ÷ t. A1: a = 350 m s⁻².', 3, NULL, NULL),
('5fa6593d-5cbc-57e9-97f4-8cce652480f8', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '5e4207c2-e358-4374-b5ab-92bbcb2b87e7', 'a-level', '2.4', '9702 coursebook 2.4 · Deducing acceleration', 32, 32, 'A v–t graph rises from 0 to 8.0 m s⁻¹ in 4.0 s and then from 8.0 m s⁻¹ to 12 m s⁻¹ in the next 4.0 s (both straight). Calculate the change in acceleration between the two stages.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '1', 'm s⁻²', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'a₁ = 8.0 ÷ 4.0 = 2.0 m s⁻²; a₂ = 4.0 ÷ 4.0 = 1.0 m s⁻²; change = 2.0 − 1.0 = 1.0 m s⁻². Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: both gradients. C1: difference. A1: Δa = 1.0 m s⁻².', 3, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fge4124b5e-t fge4124b5e-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fge4124b5e-t">Two gradients</title><desc id="fge4124b5e-d">A v–t graph rising from 0 to 8.0 m s⁻¹ in 4.0 s and then from 8.0 to 12 m s⁻¹ in the next 4.0 s.</desc><line x1="29.4" y1="34" x2="29.4" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="68.6" y1="34" x2="68.6" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="107.8" y1="34" x2="107.8" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="147" y1="34" x2="147" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="186.1" y1="34" x2="186.1" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="225.3" y1="34" x2="225.3" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="264.5" y1="34" x2="264.