('f9798ef7-5578-5314-9a4b-7415bb0888b4', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '5e4207c2-e358-4374-b5ab-92bbcb2b87e7', 'a-level', '2.4', '9702 coursebook 2.4 · Deducing acceleration', 35, 35, 'A tangent to a v–t curve at t = 10 s passes through (4.0 s, 0 m s⁻¹) and (16 s, 30 m s⁻¹). The velocity at 10 s is 17 m s⁻¹. Calculate the acceleration at 10 s, and state whether the tangent is above or below the curve point. Give the acceleration.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '2.5', 'm s⁻²', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'a = (30 − 0) ÷ (16 − 4.0) = 2.5 m s⁻². The tangent at 10 s gives 15 m s⁻¹ there, below 17 m s⁻¹, so it was drawn wrongly or the reading is off. Mark scheme (4 marks). M1: tangent gradient. C1: value. C1: check. A1: a = 2.5 m s⁻².', 4, NULL, NULL),
('9ad895c7-9bbc-55e8-bef0-58601ad725e5', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '5e4207c2-e358-4374-b5ab-92bbcb2b87e7', 'a-level', '2.4', '9702 coursebook 2.4 · Deducing acceleration', 36, 36, 'A v–t graph has negative velocity and a positive gradient. What is the object doing?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'Moving in the negative direction and slowing down', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Acceleration opposes velocity. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: negative direction. C1: slowing. A1: A (Moving in the negative direction and slowing down).', 3, NULL, NULL),
