('cba70367-5b56-5229-b3fa-0ad621bdf56b', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', '5e4207c2-e358-4374-b5ab-92bbcb2b87e7', 'a-level', '2.4', '9702 coursebook 2.4 · Deducing acceleration', 51, 51, 'A rocket''s v–t graph is a straight line from 0 to 400 m s⁻¹ in 20 s, then a straight line falling with gradient −9.81 m s⁻². (a) Calculate the gradient of the first part. (b) Calculate the time after burnout at which the graph reaches v = 0.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '40.77', 's', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) 400 ÷ 20 = 20 m s⁻². (b) t = 400 ÷ 9.81 = 40.8 s. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: gradient. C1: value. M1: t = v/g. C1: value. A1: t = 40.8 s.', 5, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg491823a4-t fg491823a4-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg491823a4-t">Rocket</title><desc id="fg491823a4-d">A rocket v–t graph rising to 400 m s⁻¹ in 20 s and then falling in a straight line with gradient −9.81 m s⁻² to zero.</desc><line x1="36.2" y1="34" x2="36.2" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="85.6" y1="34" x2="85.6" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="135" y1="34" x2="135" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="184.4" y1="34" x2="184.4" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="233.8" y1="34" x2="233.8" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="283.2" y1="34" x2="283.2" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stro