('57dc008d-d151-5845-9f52-847dfd6b94ad', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', 'c47dfb2d-b9eb-482e-b89f-aecbc8e799cc', 'a-level', '2.5', '9702 coursebook 2.5 · Deducing displacement', 31, 31, 'A v–t graph rises in a straight line from 6.0 m s⁻¹ to 18 m s⁻¹ over 8.0 s. Calculate the average velocity.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '12', 'm s⁻¹', false, NULL, false, NULL, 's = (6.0 + 18) ÷ 2 × 8.0 = 96 m; average v = 96 ÷ 8.0 = 12 m s⁻¹. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: area. C1: ÷ time. A1: v = 12 m s⁻¹.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('315c237f-45d1-5488-a96b-f95bc9d2d452', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', 'c47dfb2d-b9eb-482e-b89f-aecbc8e799cc', 'a-level', '2.5', '9702 coursebook 2.5 · Deducing displacement', 32, 32, 'For uniform acceleration, why is the average velocity (u + v)/2?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'The v–t graph is a straight line, so the area equals the mean of u and v times t', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'The trapezium area is ½(u + v)t. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: straight line. C1: trapezium. A1: C (The v–t graph is a straight line, so the area equals the mean of u and v times t).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('9766682b-1da2-5064-80a3-25382f3bbc5d', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', 'c47dfb2d-b9eb-482e-b89f-aecbc8e799cc', 'a-level', '2.5', '9702 coursebook 2.5 · Deducing displacement', 33, 33, 'Each large square on a v–t graph is 5.0 m s⁻¹ by 2.0 s. The area under a curve is about 13.5 large squares. Estimate the displacement.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '135', 'm', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'One square = 5.0 × 2.0 = 10 m; s = 13.5 × 10 = 135 m. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: square value. C1: total. A1: s = 135 m.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('31f270d1-5f37-5fc5-bc1c-5fd264563705', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', 'c47dfb2d-b9eb-482e-b89f-aecbc8e799cc', 'a-level', '2.5', '9702 coursebook 2.5 · Deducing displacement', 34, 34, 'A lift (up positive) rises at 2.0 m s⁻¹ for 12 s, waits for 5.0 s, then descends at 2.5 m s⁻¹ for 6.0 s (ignore acceleration times). Calculate its final displacement.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '9', 'm', false, NULL, false, NULL, 's = 2.0 × 12 − 2.5 × 6.0 = 9.0 m above the start. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: up area. C1: down area subtracted. A1: s = 9.0 m.', 3, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fge3ec72f9-t fge3ec72f9-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fge3ec72f9-t">Lift up and down</title><desc id="fge3ec72f9-d">A simplified lift v–t graph: +2.0 m s⁻¹ for 12 s, zero for 5.0 s, −2.5 m s⁻¹ for 6.0 s.</desc><line x1="29.4" y1="34" x2="29.4" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="88.2" y1="34" x2="88.2" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="147" y1="34" x2="147" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="205.7" y1="34" x2="205.7" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="264.5" y1="34" x2="264.5" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="323.2" y1="34" x2="323.2" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="382" y1="34" x2="382" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9