('98f55cfe-7c8f-509e-b7ca-233d5fb5687f', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', 'c47dfb2d-b9eb-482e-b89f-aecbc8e799cc', 'a-level', '2.5', '9702 coursebook 2.5 · Deducing displacement', 37, 37, 'A curved v–t graph rises from 0. Which estimate of displacement is better: counting squares or using a single triangle from the origin to the end point?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'Counting squares, because the triangle ignores the curvature', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Counting squares follows the real curve. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: curve ≠ straight line. C1: squares more accurate. A1: A (Counting squares, because the triangle ignores the curvature).', 3, NULL, NULL),
