('aa92334a-c3ca-5c06-b872-43a35a318b11', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', 'c47dfb2d-b9eb-482e-b89f-aecbc8e799cc', 'a-level', '2.5', '9702 coursebook 2.5 · Deducing displacement', 41, 41, 'An object''s velocity is v = 2.0 + 1.5t (m s⁻¹) for 0 ≤ t ≤ 6.0 s. Calculate the displacement in the 6.0 s from the area under its v–t graph.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '39', 'm', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'v(6.0) = 2.0 + 1.5 × 6.0 = 11 m s⁻¹; s = (2.0 + 11) ÷ 2 × 6.0 = 39 m. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: final velocity. C1: trapezium. A1: s = 39 m.', 3, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg2b8a73b5-t fg2b8a73b5-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg2b8a73b5-t">v = 2.0 + 1.5t</title><desc id="fg2b8a73b5-d">The line v = 2.0 + 1.5t from 0 to 6.0 s, with the area under it shaded.</desc><line x1="29.4" y1="34" x2="29.4" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="88.2" y1="34" x2="88.2" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="147" y1="34" x2="147" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="205.7" y1="34" x2="205.7" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="264.5" y1="34" x2="264.5" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="323.2" y1="34" x2="323.2" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="382" y1="34" x2="382" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:r