('02cb663f-d5f7-56da-9727-d8322b40cdb4', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', 'c47dfb2d-b9eb-482e-b89f-aecbc8e799cc', 'a-level', '2.5', '9702 coursebook 2.5 · Deducing displacement', 44, 44, 'A car accelerates uniformly from rest to 20 m s⁻¹ in 8.0 s, travels at 20 m s⁻¹ for 30 s, then decelerates uniformly to rest in 5.0 s. (a) Calculate the total distance. (b) Calculate the average speed.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '16.98', 'm s⁻¹', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) s = 0.5 × 20 × 8.0 + 20 × 30 + 0.5 × 20 × 5.0 = 730 m. (b) v = 730 ÷ 43 = 17.0 m s⁻¹. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: triangle areas. C1: rectangle. C1: total. M1: ÷ total time. A1: v = 17.0 m s⁻¹.', 5, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fgee954c50-t fgee954c50-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fgee954c50-t">Car journey</title><desc id="fgee954c50-d">A v–t graph rising to 20 m s⁻¹ in 8.0 s, constant for 30 s, falling to zero in 5.0 s, with the area shaded.</desc><line x1="29.4" y1="34" x2="29.4" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="107.8" y1="34" x2="107.8" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="186.1" y1="34" x2="186.1" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="264.5" y1="34" x2="264.5" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="342.8" y1="34" x2="342.8" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="29.4" y1="242" x2="382" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-l