('98d140fb-0fb4-57e5-9894-b02abc099411', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', 'c47dfb2d-b9eb-482e-b89f-aecbc8e799cc', 'a-level', '2.5', '9702 coursebook 2.5 · Deducing displacement', 45, 45, 'A ball is thrown up at 14 m s⁻¹ from the edge of a cliff and lands at the bottom moving at 26 m s⁻¹ (up positive; g = 9.81 m s⁻²). (a) Calculate the time to the top. (b) Calculate the total time of flight. (c) Use areas under the v–t graph to find the cliff height.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '24.46', 'm', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) 14 ÷ 9.81 = 1.427 s. (b) Total = (14 + 26) ÷ 9.81 = 4.077 s. (c) Area below − area above = 0.5 × 26 × 2.650 − 0.5 × 14 × 1.427 = 24.5 m. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: time up. C1: total time. M1: area above. M1: net area. C1: value. A1: h = 24.5 m.', 6, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg1911374b-t fg1911374b-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg1911374b-t">Ball thrown from a cliff</title><desc id="fg1911374b-d">A straight v–t line from +14 m s⁻¹ to −26 m s⁻¹ (up positive), gradient −9.81 m s⁻²; areas above and below the axis are shaded.</desc><line x1="36.2" y1="34" x2="36.2" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="113" y1="34" x2="113" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="189.9" y1="34" x2="189.9" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="266.7" y1="34" x2="266.7" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="343.6" y1="34" x2="343.6" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:roun