('85d471e2-5257-517d-aedc-38a4ed0353ad', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', 'c47dfb2d-b9eb-482e-b89f-aecbc8e799cc', 'a-level', '2.5', '9702 coursebook 2.5 · Deducing displacement', 47, 47, 'A lift (up positive) accelerates from rest at 1.0 m s⁻² for 3.0 s, moves at constant speed for 10 s and decelerates at 1.5 m s⁻² to rest. (a) Calculate the maximum speed. (b) Calculate the braking time. (c) Calculate the height risen from the v–t graph.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '37.5', 'm', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) v = 1.0 × 3.0 = 3.0 m s⁻¹. (b) t = 3.0 ÷ 1.5 = 2.0 s. (c) h = 0.5 × 3.0 × 3.0 + 3.0 × 10 + 0.5 × 3.0 × 2.0 = 37.5 m. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: speed. C1: braking time. M1: sum of areas. C1: substitution. C1: value. A1: h = 37.5 m.', 6, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg20cf3818-t fg20cf3818-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg20cf3818-t">Lift height</title><desc id="fg20cf3818-d">A lift v–t graph rising to 3.0 m s⁻¹ in 3.0 s, constant for 10 s, falling to zero in 2.0 s, with the area shaded.</desc><line x1="24" y1="34" x2="24" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="68.8" y1="34" x2="68.8" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="113.5" y1="34" x2="113.5" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="158.2" y1="34" x2="158.2" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="203" y1="34" x2="203" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="247.8" y1="34" x2="247.8