('7882715f-4ed5-5b7f-b804-6c23badefa9e', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', 'c47dfb2d-b9eb-482e-b89f-aecbc8e799cc', 'a-level', '2.5', '9702 coursebook 2.5 · Deducing displacement', 49, 49, 'A train must travel 2.0 km between stations, accelerating uniformly at 0.50 m s⁻² to 20 m s⁻¹, cruising, then braking uniformly at 1.0 m s⁻². (a) Calculate the accelerating and braking distances. (b) Calculate the cruising time. (c) Calculate the total time.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '130', 's', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) 0.5 × 20 × 40 = 400 m (40 s); 0.5 × 20 × 20 = 200 m (20 s). (b) (2000 − 400 − 200) ÷ 20 = 70 s. (c) 40 + 70 + 20 = 130 s. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: accelerating distance. C1: braking distance. M1: remaining at 20 m s⁻¹. C1: cruise time. C1: total. A1: t = 130 s.', 6, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fgd3cd7d6b-t fgd3cd7d6b-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fgd3cd7d6b-t">Between stations</title><desc id="fgd3cd7d6b-d">A trapezium-shaped v–t graph: up to 20 m s⁻¹ in 40 s, cruising, and down to rest in 20 s.</desc><line x1="29.4" y1="34" x2="29.4" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="79.8" y1="34" x2="79.8" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="130.2" y1="34" x2="130.2" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="180.5" y1="34" x2="180.5" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="230.9" y1="34" x2="230.9" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1=