('e04b02d7-9f75-5eb7-ac16-02f52ecaaf1a', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', 'c47dfb2d-b9eb-482e-b89f-aecbc8e799cc', 'a-level', '2.5', '9702 coursebook 2.5 · Deducing displacement', 52, 52, 'A car travelling at 25 m s⁻¹ sees an obstacle 60 m ahead. The driver reacts in 0.50 s and brakes at 7.0 m s⁻². (a) Calculate the thinking distance. (b) Calculate the braking distance. (c) Decide whether the car stops in time; give the stopping distance.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '57.14', 'm', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) 25 × 0.50 = 12.5 m. (b) t = 25 ÷ 7.0 = 3.571 s; area = 0.5 × 25 × 3.571 = 44.64 m. (c) Total = 12.5 + 44.64 = 57.1 m, more than 60 m, so it does not stop in time. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: thinking. C1: braking. C1: total. B1: conclusion. A1: s = 57.1 m.', 5, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fgc0b6d966-t fgc0b6d966-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fgc0b6d966-t">Stopping in time?</title><desc id="fgc0b6d966-d">A v–t graph constant at 25 m s⁻¹ for 0.50 s and then falling to zero with gradient −7.0 m s⁻², with the area shaded.</desc><line x1="29.4" y1="34" x2="29.4" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="107.8" y1="34" x2="107.8" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="186.1" y1="34" x2="186.1" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="264.5" y1="34" x2="264.5" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="342.8" y1="34" x2="342.8" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoi