('16fb1280-6712-5127-8777-e76536f0f788', 'ec015167-65fb-47df-b565-1055132ab4f3', 'c47dfb2d-b9eb-482e-b89f-aecbc8e799cc', 'a-level', '2.5', '9702 coursebook 2.5 · Deducing displacement', 53, 53, 'Cyclist A starts from rest, accelerates at 1.0 m s⁻² for 10 s and then rides at constant speed. Cyclist B rides at a steady 8.0 m s⁻¹ from the same start at the same time. (a) Find the displacement of each after 20 s. (b) Calculate how far B is ahead.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '10', 'm', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) A: 0.5 × 10 × 10 + 10 × 10 = 150 m; B: 8.0 × 20 = 160 m. (b) 160 − 150 = 10 m. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: A. C1: B. M1: difference. C1: value. A1: Δs = 10 m.', 5, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 290" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg575e34f0-t fg575e34f0-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg575e34f0-t">Two cyclists</title><desc id="fg575e34f0-d">v–t graphs: A rising from rest at 1.0 m s⁻² to 10 m s⁻¹ at 10 s then constant; B constant at 8.0 m s⁻¹.</desc><line x1="29.4" y1="34" x2="29.4" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="117.6" y1="34" x2="117.6" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="205.7" y1="34" x2="205.7" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="293.9" y1="34" x2="293.9" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="382" y1="34" x2="382" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="29.4" y1="242" x2="382" y2="242" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-